I have a complete picture. Note an important finding: the implementation in `OwnerMapper.java` is out of sync with the current spec (`openapi.yml`) and the test — the spec/test use a points-based formula (including household and a `membershipPoints` field) that the mapper does not yet implement.

## Build system & running tests

- Build system: Maven (`/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml`; wrapper `./mvnw`). No Gradle files.
- Run all tests: `./mvnw test` (or `./mvnw verify`) from `/home/daniel/sandbox`. Uses default Surefire via the Spring Boot parent; no custom Surefire/Failsafe config in the pom.
- Run just the membership test: `./mvnw test -Dtest=AcceptanceTest`

## 1. Class/method computing membership level from factors

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — the MapStruct interface `OwnerMapper`, hand-written `default` method `toMembershipLevel(Owner owner)` (wired in via `@Mapping(target = "membershipLevel", expression = "java(toMembershipLevel(owner))")` on `toOwnerDto`).

Current implementation (lines 102-127):

```java
default Integer toMembershipLevel(Owner owner) {
    int level = 1;
    boolean hasEmail = owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank();
    if (hasEmail) {
        level++;
    }
    boolean unique = owner.getNamesakeCount() != null && owner.getNamesakeCount() == 0;
    if (unique) {
        level++;
    }
    // Pre-tenure factors cap at level 3; level 4 requires tenure over 365 days.
    level = Math.min(level, 3);
    java.time.LocalDate registrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();
    if (registrationDate != null && java.time.temporal.ChronoUnit.DAYS
            .between(registrationDate, java.time.LocalDate.now()) > 365) {
        level++;
    }
    return level;
}
```

Key mismatch: this method computes a level directly (email +1, namesakeCount==0 +1, cap 3, tenure>365d +1). It does NOT use `householdSize`, and there is no `membershipPoints` computation — but the spec and test now require a points-based model including household. So the mapper is the thing that needs updating to match the spec. Household size is available on the model via `owner.getHouseholdSize()` (populated by `AssignHouseholdSize`, see `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHouseholdSize.java`).

The full mapper also computes related derived fields (`membershipNumber`, `checkDigit`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`, `ageBand`, `telephoneDisplay`) via other `default` methods in the same file.

## 2. DTOs / response objects with membershipLevel

The `OwnerDto` is code-generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec (there is no hand-written DTO on disk; the mapper imports `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto.OwnerDto`). The field definitions live in:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, schema `Owner` (starts line 2070). Current relevant fields:

- `namesakeCount` (line 2125): int, ≥0, readOnly.
- `membershipPoints` (line 2139): int, ≥0, readOnly. Description: start at 0; +2 email present; +1 when namesakeCount==0; +2 for household of 3+ (householdSize ≥ 3); +3 for tenure over 365 days.
- `membershipLevel` (line 2147): int, 1-4, readOnly. Description: derived from membershipPoints — 1 (0-1 pts), 2 (2-3 pts), 3 (4-5 pts), 4 (6+ pts).

Important: the spec currently defines BOTH `membershipPoints` and a points-derived `membershipLevel`, but `OwnerMapper` only maps `membershipLevel` (old direct formula) and has no `membershipPoints` mapping. The domain model `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java` holds the raw factors: `email` (line 52), `registrationDate` (58), `namesakeCount` (70, `getNamesakeCount()`), `householdSize` (73, `getHouseholdSize()`), plus `householdId` (67).

## 3. Test files covering membership level logic

Only one test asserts membership behavior, plus its base class:

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` (full content, 20 lines):

```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.acceptance;

import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import static org.springframework.test.web.servlet.result.MockMvcResultMatchers.jsonPath;
import tools.jackson.databind.node.ObjectNode;

/** membership-points: points = +2 email, +1 namesake 0, +2 household of 3+, +3 tenure over
 * 365 days; mapped to level 1 (0-1) / 2 (2-3) / 3 (4-5) / 4 (6+). A fresh owner with an email and
 * no namesake scores 3 points (2 + 1), a single-member household, zero tenure -> level 2. */
class AcceptanceTest extends AcceptanceBase {

	@Test
	void coreReturnsPointsAndLevel() throws Exception {
		ObjectNode o = withPostcode(ownerNode());
		o.put("email", uniqueEmail());
		int id = createOwnerOk(o);
		getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.membershipPoints").value(3))
				.andExpect(jsonPath("$.membershipLevel").value(2));
	}
}
```

- `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java` — the `@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, `@Transactional`, `@WithMockUser` base with all the helpers used above (`ownerNode()`, `withPostcode()`, `uniqueEmail()`, `createOwnerOk()`, `getOwner()`, etc.). Full content is 322 lines; it is a black-box MockMvc harness hitting `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}`. It contains no membership-specific assertions itself but supplies the fixtures. The third test file, `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java`, is unrelated (audit-log capture support).

The test expects `$.membershipPoints`==3 and `$.membershipLevel`==2 for a fresh owner with email + unique name (email +2, namesake 0 +1 = 3 points → level 2). The current `OwnerMapper` would instead return `membershipLevel`==3 (email +1, unique +1 = level 3) and no `membershipPoints` field at all — so `coreReturnsPointsAndLevel` would currently fail. This confirms `OwnerMapper.toMembershipLevel` (and a missing `toMembershipPoints`) is the code that needs to be brought in line with the spec/test.

This is a project using OfficeFloor functions (under `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/`) for the create pipeline, but the membership scoring itself lives entirely in the MapStruct `OwnerMapper`, not in an OfficeFloor function.

